//! The `fill-opacity` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property defines the
//! opacity of the painting operation (color, gradient, pattern, etc.) applied to SVG shapes or text
//! content elements to fill the element. The property defines the opacity of the element's `fill`
//! only; it does not affect the stroke. If present, it overrides the element's `fill-opacity`
//! attribute.
//!
//! Initial: 1. Inherited: yes.
//! Percentages: map to the range [0,1].
//!
//! Grammar: <'opacity'>
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/fill-stroke-3/#propdef-fill-opacity
//!
//! Author guide: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/fill-opacity
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
//!
//! Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.

